"donor_lfcse":0.0865502,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-2.5298e-07},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_symbol":"NDST1","gene_symbol_current":"NDST1","gene_id":"ENSG00000070614","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":true,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":1.26742e-07,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.0932472,"nucleus_score":-5.44099,"pct_ad":0.354054,"pct_control":0.374115,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.974227,"donor_log2fc":-0.0221074,"donor_lfcse":0.10497,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-0.00169833}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"Ast","gene_id":"ENSG00000070614","module":"yellow","kme":0.198755,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.506562,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Ex","gene_id":"ENSG00000070614","module":"blue","kme":0.146313,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.391996,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_id":"ENSG00000070614","module":"blue","kme":0.177671,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.842971,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000070614","entrez_id":["3340"],"uniprot":["P52848"],"ncbi_summary":"This gene encodes a member of the heparan sulfate/heparin GlcNAc N-deacetylase/ N-sulfotransferase family. The encoded enzyme is a type II transmembrane protein that resides in the Golgi apparatus. The encoded protein catalyzes the transfer of sulfate from 3'-phosphoadenosine 5'-phosphosulfate to nitrogen of glucosamine in heparan sulfate. Alternative splicing results in multiple transcript variants. [provided by RefSeq, Dec 2014].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"P52848","text":"[Isoform 1]: Essential bifunctional enzyme that catalyzes both the N-deacetylation and the N-sulfation of glucosamine (GlcNAc) of the glycosaminoglycan in heparan sulfate (PubMed:35137078, PubMed:9230113, PubMed:9744796). Modifies the GlcNAc-GlcA disaccharide repeating sugar backbone to make N-sulfated heparosan, a prerequisite substrate for later modifications in heparin biosynthesis (PubMed:9230113). Plays a role in determining the extent and pattern of sulfation of heparan sulfate. Participates in biosynthesis of heparan sulfate that can ultimately serve as L-selectin ligands, thereby playing a role in inflammatory response (By similarity). Required for the exosomal release of SDCBP, CD63 and syndecan (PubMed:22660413). [Isoform 3]: Lacks both N-deacetylase and N-sulfotransferase activities. Acts as a dominant negative on isoform 1, likely by changing the composition of enzyme complexes responsible for elongation and modification of heparan sulfates."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}